cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cubic Time Dilation Model for Enhanced GNSS"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
abstract: >-
  "Cubic Time Dilation Model for Enhanced GNSS Accuracy and Security" (proposal,
  September 2024) and its 2nd-edition revision, together with Module VI ("Cubic
  time dilation") extracted standalone from the Chronowave Dynamics Temporal
  Engine compendium. The original proposed replacing the traditional Lorentz
  exponent -1/2 with a cube-root exponent -1/3 on the strength of 1,000
  simulations against live constellation data; the 2nd edition documents that
  this exponent has since been excluded by independent measurement and verifies
  every remaining claim against a Python backend checked against published
  values (Ashby 2003, ICD-GPS-200). v1.1.0 fixes issues an independent review
  found in the revision itself, including a misdated chronology of the
  exclusion evidence and an overstated degeneracy argument.
